      },
      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/1/12/5109",
      "text": [
        ": قُلْتُ لَهُ رَجُلٌ سَرَقَ مِنَ اَلْمَغْنَمِ اَلشَّيْءَ اَلَّذِي يَجِبُ عَلَيْهِ اَلْقَطْعُ قَالَ \"يُنْظَرُ كَمِ اَلَّذِي يُصِيبُهُ فَإِنْ كَانَ اَلَّذِي أَخَذَ أَقَلَّ مِنْ نَصِيبِهِ عُزِّرَ وَ دُفِعَ إِلَيْهِ تَمَامُ مَالِهِ وَ إِنْ كَانَ أَخَذَ مِثْلَ اَلَّذِي لَهُ فَلاَ شَيْءَ عَلَيْهِ وَ إِنْ كَانَ أَخَذَ فَضْلاً بِقَدْرِ ثَمَنِ مِجَنٍّ وَ هُوَ رُبُعُ دِينَارٍ قُطِعَ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5109 - Yunus narrated from Abdullah ibn Sinan from Abu Abdullah (as) who said:\nI asked Imam (as) about a man who stole from the war spoils an amount that would normally require his hand to be cut off.\nImam (as) said: \"It should be examined how much his rightful share is. If what he took was less than his portion, he is to be disciplined (ta'zir) and given the remainder of his share.\nIf he took exactly what was due to him, then there is nothing upon him.\nBut if he took more than his share equal to the value of a shield, which is a quarter of a dinar, then his hand is to be cut off.\""
        ]
      }
    },
